    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, from the framework layer through persistence. I've labeled each step **[V]** (validation/rejection gate) or **[S]** (side-effect: mutation, derived field, persistence, or log).\n\n## Before the controller body runs (Spring framework)\n\n1. **[V] Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` on `addOwner`. Caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role or the request is rejected.\n2. **[S] Deserialization** \u2014 Jackson binds the JSON body into an `OwnerFieldsDto`.\n3. **[V] Bean Validation on the body** (`@Valid` in `OwnersApi.addOwner`). All of the following fire together; any failure \u2192 400:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (letters, 1\u20133 words), `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (letters, optional trailing `.`), `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (non-blank), `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (AU/E.164 shapes), `@Size(1..25)`\n   - `address` / `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` \u2014 each (when present) `@Pattern` (non-blank), `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`, plus `@DisposableEmailValidation` (domain not in the `mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail` blocklist)\n   - `registrationDate` \u2014 `@PastOrPresent`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern` (exactly 4 digits)\n   - **Class-level `@AddressRequired`** \u2014 either `addressLine1` or `address` must be present/non-blank\n   - **Class-level `@PostcodeValidation`** \u2014 a 4-digit postcode must fall in the city's region range (Sydney 2000\u20132099, Melbourne 3000\u20133099, Brisbane 4000\u20134099; unknown cities accept any)\n\n## Inside `addOwner` (controller body)\n\n4. **[S] Idempotency short-circuit** \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` request header; if that key was already used, returns the *previously* created owner with **200 OK** and does nothing else (no new entity, no side-effects below).\n5. **[S] DTO \u2192 `Owner` mapping** (`OwnerMapper.toOwner`), whose setters apply normalization side-effects; `id` and `pets` are ignored:\n   - `setTelephone` \u2192 `TelephoneNumber.toE164` (strips punctuation, forces `+61`/`+` E.164 form)\n   - `setEmail` \u2192 lowercased\n   - `setAddress` / `setAddressLine1` / `setAddressLine2` \u2192 `PostalAddress.normalize` (trim, collapse whitespace, uppercase, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`)\n6. **[S] `setHouseholdId`** \u2192 `Households.idFor` (12-hex-char SHA-256 of normalized `lastName` + `postcode`).\n7. **[S] Load existing owners** \u2014 `findAllOwners()`, filtered to exclude soft-deleted ones. This filtered collection feeds every check below.\n8. **[S] `setRegistrationDate`** \u2192 `BusinessDays.effective` (defaults to today if null, then rolls forward off weekends and listed 2026 holidays to the next business day).\n9. **[V] Daily-volume cap** \u2014 if \u2265 **100** existing owners already share this registration date \u2192 **429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS**.\n10. **[V] Identity duplicate** \u2014 `Identities.isDuplicate`: another owner has the same full identity key (`normalizedTelephone|email|householdId`) \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**.\n11. **[V] Household duplicate** \u2014 `Households.isDuplicate`: an existing owner is already in this household (same `householdId`), *unless* `sharesHousehold == true` \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**.\n12. **[V] City cap** \u2014 `CityCodes.countInCity` \u2265 **50** existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive) \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**.\n13. **[S] `setHouseholdMemberCount`** \u2192 `Households.size` (existing housemates + 1).\n14. **[S] `assignCustomerCode`** \u2192 `CustomerCodes.uniqueFor`: builds `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode, hash of `telephone+lastName`) and appends `-n` (n\u22652) until unique among existing codes.\n15. **[S] `setNamesakeCount`** \u2192 `Namesakes.count` (existing owners with same first + last name, case-insensitive).\n16. **[S] `setBulkSignupWarning`** \u2192 `BulkSignups.exceededDailyLimit` (true when > **80** existing owners share the registration date).\n17. **[S] `setPossibleDuplicateOf`** \u2192 `PossibleDuplicates.matchId`: id of an existing owner with same `lastName` + `postcode` but a *different* telephone (null when `sharesHousehold == true`).\n18. **[S] Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`. On persistence:\n    - `@PrePersist defaultRegistrationDate` \u2014 no-op here (date already set in step 8).\n    - `@PostPersist OwnerAuditListener.onCreate` \u2014 writes an `AUDIT` log line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, membership level and membership number.\n19. **[S] Remember idempotency** \u2014 `IdempotencyKeys.remember(key, owner)` stores the result under the header key for future replays.\n20. **[S] Build response** \u2014 `toOwnerDto` computes derived fields (salutation, initials, membershipNumber, fiscalYear, checkDigit, membership points/level, locality, timezone, contactPreference, ageBand, telephoneDisplay, selfLink, displayName), sets the `Location` header, and returns **201 CREATED**.\n\nTwo things worth flagging: the entire body (steps 4\u201320) is **not** annotated `@Transactional` (unlike `deleteOwner`), and the duplicate/cap checks in steps 9\u201312 read a non-transactional `findAllOwners()` snapshot, so they are subject to races under concurrent creates."
